       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and the FDA label caps a single dose at about 850\u20131,000 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO twice daily**, which is a more typical starting or maintenance dose.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical reason. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
