       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the safety problem. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose, and 1700 mg is about twice the maximum single dose. You also haven't given a clinical reason for exceeding those limits, and I can't verify one. The risk is serious harm, specifically metformin-associated lactic acidosis.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Give me the dose and frequency, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Go through pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this dose is warranted, a pharmacist or attending can review it and enter or co-sign it directly.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** If the dose came from a note or a verbal order, it may be worth confirming the source. 1700 mg may be a mistake for 850 mg or 1000 mg."
      }
